<title>USA: King World no longer on block - WSJ.</title>
<headline>King World no longer on block - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>King World Productions Inc is no longer for sale and is planning to announce a dividend and five million share buyback program today, the Wall Street Journal said in Tuesday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>Company Chairman Roger King was quoted in the newspaper as saying moves were aimed at showing King World was focused on growing, not selling out.</p>
<p>The company is expected to report second quarter earnings of $0.97 per share or $36.7 million compared to $0.93 per share or $35.2 million, the paper said.</p>
<p>The Journal said King World's board approved a special dividend of $2-a-share payable on May 16.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>(New York newsdesk 212-859-1610)</p>
